            <ArticleTitle>The painful mouth.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>935-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">The painful mouth presents a diagnostic challenge to the general practitioner. Despite curriculum revision of most medical courses, oro-pharyngeal diseases are still inadequately covered.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">This article aims to alert the GP to common causes of a painful mouth and provides a guide to diagnosis and management.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="DISCUSSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Four case studies are presented to illustrate common problems presenting in general practice, and their optimal treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
